  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Shooting both ways",
  "description": "Two goals with keepers, about 25–30 metres apart. Blue line up at an angle by one goal and red by the other, everyone with a ball, and both teams go at the same time. The first player runs round a cone out on the pitch, the next in line passes, and the runner shoots first time. Fetch your ball and join the back. Which team scores most in three minutes?\n\nVariation: swap the cone for a wall player. The first player dribbles out, plays a one-two and shoots. Slightly older players can instead receive a long pass from the line at the other end, control it and shoot. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "See where the keeper is before the ball arrives."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Pass with the inside of the foot, in front of the runner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Use the laces for power and the inside of the foot for accuracy."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Follow up your shot – the keeper might spill it."
    }
  ],
